
/* Built-in homebrew pack (M17: moved here from pack.js). Same shape as a pasted pack, see PACK_TEMPLATE in pack.js */
var HB_BUILTIN={retromistika:{id:"retromistika",name:"Retromistika (Homebrew)",desc:"Valeria's Fieldbook of Retromistika (Playtest): Mistikan and Retron species, 7 subclasses, Bleeding, Burning, and Jinxed conditions, Automotive and Computer skills. Setting: 80s Indonesia and Nusantara mysticism, AD 485.",
 species:{
  Mistikan:{size:"Medium",speed:30,dark:0,skills:["Nature"],lin:{label:"Ecocentric Ancestry",opts:["Kalnis Ancestry (sky)","Buana Ancestry (land)","Shia Ancestry (sea)"]},linFx:{"Buana":{speedSet:35,senses:[["Tremorsense",15,"Land Treader",""]]},"Shia":{senses:[["Blindsight",30,"Sonar Sense","Only while at least half of your body is underwater."]]},"Kalnis":{fly:["walk","Sky Step: a Bonus Action gives you this Fly Speed until the end of your turn"]}},linText:{"Kalnis Ancestry (sky)": "The sky of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Sky Step.** You can take a Bonus Action to give yourself a Fly Speed that matches your Speed and lasts until the current turn ends. **Soft Lander.** Whenever you take damage from a fall, you take only half of it. **Elusive Walker.** When you take the Dodge action or the Disengage action, you add your Proficiency Bonus to your Armor Class until the start of your next turn. You gain this bonus only when you take that action with your action, not when a Bonus Action or another feature lets you take it.", "Buana Ancestry (land)": "The land of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Land Treader.** Your base Speed becomes 35 feet, and you have Tremorsense with a range of 15 feet. **Verdant Empath.** By touching a Plant creature, you can sense or read its simple thoughts and feelings. If you talk with such a plant, it answers only by letting you feel its emotions and moods. **Arborian Armor.** As a Bonus Action, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus. As long as you still have any of these Temporary Hit Points, your Speed is 10 feet.", "Shia Ancestry (sea)": "The sea of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Amphibious.** You can breathe both air and water. **Aquatic Transport.** As a Magic action, you dissolve into a puddle of water and teleport to a flat surface you can see within 15 feet of yourself. If you are completely submerged in water when you do so, the range becomes 30 feet, and you can instead arrive in another body of water that you can see and that is large enough to hold you. **Sonar Sense.** While at least half of your body is under water, you have Blindsight with a range of 30 feet."},
   traits:[["Ecocentric Ancestry","**Ecocentric Ancestry.** The world's natural affinity still clings to you. Choose one of the following ancestries: Kalnis (sky), Buana (land), or Shia (sea). You gain every benefit of the ancestry you choose. **Kalnis Ancestry.** The sky of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Sky Step.** You can take a Bonus Action to give yourself a Fly Speed that matches your Speed and lasts until the current turn ends. **Soft Lander.** Whenever you take damage from a fall, you take only half of it. **Elusive Walker.** When you take the Dodge action or the Disengage action, you add your Proficiency Bonus to your Armor Class until the start of your next turn. You gain this bonus only when you take that action with your action, not when a Bonus Action or another feature lets you take it. **Buana Ancestry.** The land of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Land Treader.** Your base Speed becomes 35 feet, and you have Tremorsense with a range of 15 feet. **Verdant Empath.** By touching a Plant creature, you can sense or read its simple thoughts and feelings. If you talk with such a plant, it answers only by letting you feel its emotions and moods. **Arborian Armor.** As a Bonus Action, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to twice your Proficiency Bonus. As long as you still have any of these Temporary Hit Points, your Speed is 10 feet. **Shia Ancestry.** The sea of the world has given you its blessing, granting you the following benefits. **Amphibious.** You can breathe both air and water. **Aquatic Transport.** As a Magic action, you dissolve into a puddle of water and teleport to a flat surface you can see within 15 feet of yourself. If you are completely submerged in water when you do so, the range becomes 30 feet, and you can instead arrive in another body of water that you can see and that is large enough to hold you. **Sonar Sense.** While at least half of your body is under water, you have Blindsight with a range of 30 feet."],
    ["Worldly Understanding","You gain proficiency in the Nature skill."]]},
  Retron:{size:"Medium",speed:30,dark:0,opts:{label:"Domesticated Ancestry",n:2,list:[["Limited Darkvision","You have Darkvision with a range of 30 feet.",{dark:30}],["Limited Spellcaster","You learn one cantrip of your choice from the Sorcerer spell list. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for that cantrip.",{cantrip:"Sorcerer",spAb:"CHA"}],["Masterful","You gain proficiency with one weapon of your choice, and you can use the mastery property of that weapon.",{weapon:1}],["Quick","Your Speed increases by 10 feet.",{speed:10}],["Skillful","You gain proficiency in two skills of your choice.",{skills:2}],["Versatile","You gain one Origin feat of your choice.",{feat:1}]]},
   traits:[["Domesticated Ancestry","**Domesticated Ancestry.** Your lineage was shaped by the conveniences of modern living, the habits people build to make daily life easier. Choose two of the following options: Limited Darkvision, Limited Spellcaster, Masterful, Quick, Skillful, or Versatile."],["Embracing Change","Saving throws you make to avoid the Frightened condition, or to end it on yourself, have Advantage."],["Modernist","You have Advantage on any D20 Test you make to work out how a piece of technology you can see is used."]]}},
 subclasses:{
  Druid:{"Circle of the Feathers": [[3, "Avian Shape", "When you use Wild Shape to become a Beast, the form always has feathers. While you wear it, you gain these benefits. **Take Flight.** You gain a Fly Speed equal to five times your Wisdom modifier (minimum 5 feet). **Swift Glide.** Your Armor Class increases by 2. **Soft Fall.** You take only half of any falling damage."], [6, "Birds of Paradise", "While Avian Shape is active, you can pick one of these effects. **Astrapia's Splendor.** Spend a spell slot to heal every creature in a 15-foot Emanation around you. Each one regains Hit Points from a number of d6s equal to the level of the slot. **Parotia's Display.** You can cast the Druid cantrips you know and the level 1 spells you have prepared. **Standardwing's Grace.** When you take damage from a source you can see, spend a spell slot to reduce that damage by a number of d10s equal to the level of the slot."], [10, "Birds of Prey", "When you pick an option from Birds of Paradise, you can pick one of these instead. **Falcon's Dive.** If you move 20 feet in a straight line before you attack in your Wild Shape form, the attack deals extra damage from a number of d6s equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1). **Owl's Precision.** You gain Darkvision out to 120 feet, and you can see normally in darkness of any kind. You also gain Expertise in Perception and Stealth. **Hawk-Eagle's Talons.** When you take the Attack action, you make one extra attack as part of it."], [14, "Enchanted Wings", "While Avian Shape is active, you gain these benefits. **Evasive Movement.** Your Armor Class increases by another 2. **Speed Flying.** Your Fly Speed grows by 15 feet. **Flyby.** Moving out of a creature's reach with your Fly Speed never provokes Opportunity Attacks."]]},
  Paladin:{"Oath of the Law": [[3, "Oath of the Law Spells", "Once you reach a Paladin level shown below, you always have the listed spells prepared. **Paladin Level 3.** Alarm, Command. **Paladin Level 5.** See Invisibility, Zone of Truth. **Paladin Level 9.** Dispel Magic, Remove Curse. **Paladin Level 13.** Guardian of Faith, Locate Creature. **Paladin Level 17.** Legend Lore, Wall of Force."], [3, "Remote Smite", "You can cast Divine Smite after you hit a creature within 60 feet of you with a Ranged weapon."], [3, "Active Dispatch", "Your oath gives you tools for enforcing the law. **Freeze!** As a Magic action, spend one use of Channel Divinity to cast Hold Monster without a spell slot. The spell counts as a Paladin spell for you. **Cruiser.** As a Bonus Action, spend one use of Channel Divinity to call a motorcycle as your mount. You can mount it at once, or let it appear in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of you. It lasts 8 hours, until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action, or until a full minute passes without anyone riding it."], [7, "Improved Remote Smite", "When you see a creature within 60 feet of you hit another creature with a weapon attack, you can use your Reaction to cast Divine Smite, targeting the creature that was hit. You can also use this feature as a Bonus Action in the normal way when your Cruiser is the one that made the attack."], [15, "Hot Pursuit", "When a creature within 10 feet of you moves or teleports, you can move toward it, using the Speed you left unspent on your previous turn."], [20, "New Order", "As a Bonus Action, you become the embodiment of law for 1 minute. During that time, you can use a Magic action to force a creature you can see within 30 feet of you to make a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you choose one of these effects to place on it. **Weak.** Choose a damage type. Immunity to it becomes Resistance, Resistance to it is removed, and a creature with neither gains Vulnerability. **Sturdy.** Choose a damage type. The target gains Resistance to it, or Immunity if it already has Resistance. **Armored.** Its base Armor Class becomes 20. **Unarmored.** Its Armor Class becomes 10, unless it is already lower. **Aware.** It gains Blindsight, Tremorsense, and Truesight out to 60 feet. **Expert.** It gains Expertise in one skill you choose. **Unbounded.** It gains Burrow, Fly, and Swim Speeds equal to its Speed. **Nimble.** Its Speed is tripled. **Sluggish.** Its Speed becomes 5 feet, unless it is already lower. The effects last until the feature ends. You can have a number of effects active at once equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore it by spending a level 5 spell slot, which takes no action."]]},
  Sorcerer:{"Khodam Sorcery": [[3, "Manifest Spirit", "As a Bonus Action, you manifest a guardian spirit in a space within 10 feet of you. While it is present, these rules apply. **Dormant Spirit.** The spirit can move and use its Reaction on its own, but the only action it takes is Dodge, unless you command it with Empathic Strike. **Empathic Strike.** As a Magic action, spend spell slots of level 1 or higher, or Sorcery Points, to command the spirit to make a number of attacks equal to the slot level or to the Sorcery Points spent. **Mental Restraint.** You can't maintain Concentration on spells. **Mystical Bond.** When you take damage, the spirit takes the same amount. When the spirit takes damage, you take half of it instead. **Spirit Bound.** The spirit stays within a 10-foot Emanation of you and can't be forced out of it. **Spiritual Link.** The spirit's size matches yours, and its Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores equal yours. The spirit lasts until you dismiss it as a Bonus Action or you have the Unconscious condition."], [6, "Protective Blessing", "Your spirit grows stronger. **Flexible Range.** The spirit can now range within a 30-foot Emanation of you. **Spiritual Missile.** When you use Empathic Strike, you can instead target a creature you can see within 60 feet of the spirit. The creature makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, it takes half of the Force damage rolled, using a number of d12s equal to the spell slot level, or twice the number of Sorcery Points spent. **Rapid Protector.** When you are hit, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point as a Reaction to teleport the spirit to a space within 5 feet of you, so that it takes the damage instead."], [14, "Spiritual Unleash", "You and your spirit grow closer. **Distant Range.** The spirit can now range within 120 feet of you. **Autonomous Spirit.** You can maintain Concentration on spells while your spirit is present."], [18, "Incorporeal Resilience", "While your spirit is present, you have Resistance to all damage, and Immunity to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition."]]},
  Barbarian:{"Path of the Barong":[[3,"Durable Skin","Your body begins to grow as tough as the hide of a Barong, granting you the following benefits. **Strike Breaker.** If you take damage during your Rage, you can take a Reaction to spend Barbarian Hit Point Dice, up to a number equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of one), and roll them. Reduce the damage you take by the total rolled. **Armored Rage.** You gain training with Heavy armor, and wearing Heavy armor does not stop you from entering your Rage or keeping it going."],[6,"Mystical Endurance","Whenever you finish a Short Rest, you regain one of your spent Hit Point Dice. Once you reach Barbarian level 13, you regain two spent Hit Point Dice instead."],[6,"Beast of Siege","Your savagery toward your enemies turns more bestial, granting you the following benefits. **Vicious Claws.** While your Rage is active, your Unarmed Strike counts as a Simple Melee weapon. **Siege Warrior.** While your Rage is active, every melee weapon you wield has the Cleave mastery property. Cleave works as follows: after a melee attack roll with the weapon hits a creature, you can attack a second creature with it, as long as that second creature stands no more than 5 feet from the first one and is inside your reach. If that attack hits, it deals the weapon's damage to the second creature, though your ability modifier is added to this damage only when the modifier is negative. This extra attack can happen only once per turn. **Whirlwind Strike.** When you use Cleave through this feature, you can target additional creatures, up to a number equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of one)."],[10,"Guardian Beast","When an attack you can see hits a creature that you can see up to 30 feet away from you, you can take a Reaction to move up to your Speed and take that attack in its place. If the attack still hits you, your Durable Skin feature can be used as part of that same Reaction."],[14,"Indomitable Bulwark","Whenever you take damage from a source you can see, you can ignore an amount of that damage equal to your Barbarian level."]]},
  Bard:{"College of Hymns":[[3,"Spiritual Musicist","You have learned to tell the stories of the spirits through your music, granting you the following benefits. **Kecapi Adept.** You gain proficiency with the Zither, a musical instrument. **Mystical Instrumentalist.** By performing a ritual that takes 10 minutes, you can roll one of your Bard Hit Point Dice and lose Hit Points equal to the number rolled. You then gain a Zither, which can serve as your Spellcasting Focus. It lasts for 8 hours and vanishes once that time is up. You can have only one such Zither at a time. **Spiritual Rhythmist.** While you use the Zither created by Mystical Instrumentalist as your Spellcasting Focus, you have one extra use of Bardic Inspiration."],[3,"Eerie Strings","As long as you have the Zither created by your Mystical Instrumentalist feature, you can roll one additional die for the damage or healing of a spell you cast if the spell deals Thunder or Psychic damage, or if it restores Hit Points and targets an Undead creature. In addition, when you cast such a spell, you can spend one use of Bardic Inspiration and roll the Bardic Inspiration die, adding the number rolled to the damage or healing of that spell. Any creature that holds a Bardic Inspiration die from you can also use this feature."],[6,"Mystic Seer","As long as you have the Zither created by your Mystical Instrumentalist feature, you can play it as a Magic action, which gives you the Blinded condition for 1 hour. For that hour, you gain the following benefits. **Blind Vision.** Attack rolls against you do not have Advantage because of your Blinded condition. **Spirit Seer.** You have Blindsight, and you can see into the Ethereal Plane, out to a number of feet equal to your Charisma modifier multiplied by ten (minimum of 10 feet). Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Short Rest or a Long Rest."],[14,"Persistent Song","When you are maintaining Concentration on a spell and fail the Constitution saving throw to keep it, you can spend one use of Bardic Inspiration to turn the failure into a success. Any creature that holds a Bardic Inspiration die from you can also use this feature."]]},
  Fighter:{"Pencak Silat":[[3,"Close Quarter Combatant","You have shaped your fighting style to be most dangerous at close range with weapons that are easy to hide, granting you the following benefits. **Cunning Eye.** You gain proficiency in your choice of the Perception or Medicine skill. **Unarmed Combatant.** When you roll damage for your Unarmed Strike, you can roll 1d6 in place of its normal damage. If you aren't holding a Shield, the die becomes a d8 instead. **Flowing Blades.** When you deal damage with a Dagger, a Sickle, or a Shortsword, you can use your Unarmed Strike damage die in place of the weapon's normal damage die."],[7,"Martial Stances","As an action or a Bonus Action (your choice), you can enter one of the stances described below. You can switch to the other stance by taking an action or a Bonus Action (your choice). **Offensive Stance.** One time on each of your turns, after your melee weapon or Unarmed Strike hits a creature, you can spend one use of your Second Wind to Shove that creature as part of the same action. If the creature fails its saving throw against the Shove, you can make one follow-up attack against it with a melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike. If the creature succeeds on the saving throw, the use of Second Wind is not spent. **Defensive Stance.** When you are hit by a melee attack that you can see, you can spend one use of your Second Wind. Instead of regaining Hit Points, you roll 1d10 and add the result to your Armor Class against that attack, which might cause it to miss. If the attack hits anyway, the use of Second Wind is not spent."],[10,"Relentless Warrior","Your mastery of the flow of combat grows even more dangerous, granting you the following benefits. **Brutal Combatant.** Your Unarmed Strike damage die becomes a d8. It is a d10 while your hands hold no Shield. **Low Fighting Stance.** While you have the Prone condition, attack rolls against you do not have Advantage because of it. **Dauntless.** When you try to Grapple or Shove a creature, it can be up to two sizes larger than you."],[15,"Lethal Strike","Your blows now land as killing strikes rather than ordinary hits, granting you the following benefits. **Deadly Combatant.** Your Unarmed Strike damage die becomes a d10. It is a d12 while your hands hold no Shield. **Killing Blow.** If your melee weapon or Unarmed Strike hits a creature that has the Prone condition, the attack can deal an extra 1d12 damage."],[18,"Master of Pencak Silat","Your stances have become far more refined and deadly. The stances of your Martial Stances feature improve as follows. **Offensive Stance.** When the target fails its saving throw, you can make two follow-up attacks against it with a melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike, instead of one. **Defensive Stance.** If the roll changes a hit into a miss, your Armor Class keeps that bonus until your next turn begins. In addition, whenever one of your turns begins, you can switch to a different stance from your Martial Stances feature without taking an action or a Bonus Action."]]},
  Rogue:{"Joystick":[[3,"Coin Muncher","You gain proficiency with every kind of Gaming Set. Whenever you roll an ability check to win a game played with one of your Gaming Sets, you can spend 1 GP to add 1 to the d20 roll."],[3,"Round One","When you roll Initiative to enter combat, you can take a Bonus Action to make a Ranged weapon, or a Melee weapon with the Finesse property, become an Arcade Weapon for 1 minute. While this effect lasts, you gain the following benefits. **Phase One.** When you attack with an Arcade Weapon, you can use your Sneak Attack without needing Advantage on the attack roll and without needing an ally within 5 feet of the target. **Phase Two.** Once 5 rounds have passed while you wield an Arcade Weapon, you can take two Bonus Actions instead of one until the start of your next turn. You can use the extra Bonus Action only for features of the Rogue class or of your Rogue subclass. **Final Phase.** During the final round of this feature's duration, when you attack with an Arcade Weapon, you can change the weapon's damage to Force damage. In addition, if you roll 9 or lower on the d20 for the first attack roll you make on your turn, you treat the roll as a 10."],[3,"Speedrun","When you are using your Round One feature during combat, you can take a Bonus Action to advance the feature's progress by 3 rounds. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest. Starting at Rogue level 9, you can use it twice, and you regain all uses when you finish a Long Rest."],[9,"Flip the Score","When a creature makes an attack roll while it is within 5 feet of you and you can see it, you can respond with your Reaction, turning its d20 upside down and use the number on the bottom face instead. Opposite faces of a die always total one more than the highest number on the die, so for a d20 the new result is 21 minus the original roll. For example, a roll of 18 becomes a 3, since 18 plus 3 is 21. Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Short Rest or a Long Rest."],[13,"Extra Life","When you deal Sneak Attack damage, you can take a Bonus Action to give up some of your Sneak Attack d6s; the number you give up equals your Dexterity modifier (minimum of one). Roll those d6s, and regain Hit Points equal to their total instead of dealing that damage. Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Short Rest or a Long Rest."],[17,"Kill Screen","When you deal Sneak Attack damage and one of the dice shows a 6, you can roll one more d6 and add its result to that Sneak Attack damage. The number of extra d6s you can roll this way can't exceed the total number of Sneak Attack damage dice you currently have."]]},
  Monk:{"Warrior of Aerobics":[[3,"Feel the Burn","When you take the same kind of action that you took on your previous turn, you gain a benefit tied to that action, which lasts until your next turn begins. **Attack Action.** Your attack rolls and damage rolls with Melee weapons and Unarmed Strikes get a +1 bonus. **Dash Action.** Your Speed increases by 5 feet. **Disengage Action.** You gain a +1 bonus to your Armor Class. **Dodge Action.** You gain 5 Temporary Hit Points. **Help Action.** You can choose one additional creature as a target. **Hide Action.** You gain a +1 bonus to your Dexterity (Stealth) check. These benefits can stack, and the maximum number of stacks equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). The stacks reset when you take a different kind of action or when you take no action at all."],[6,"Calisthenic Exercise","You can spend 10 minutes exercising to prepare for the day's adventures. When you finish, you gain a number of Advantages equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one). Each one can be used to give yourself Advantage on one attack roll or one saving throw. Any of them you haven't used expire when you finish a Long Rest. Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Short Rest or a Long Rest."],[11,"Abs of Steel","After you use your Calisthenic Exercise feature, you have Resistance to all damage except Psychic and Force damage for as long as you still have at least one unused Advantage from that feature."],[17,"Aerobic Stars","Every bonus you gain from your Feel the Burn feature is doubled."]]},
  Warlock:{"The Leyak Queen":[[3,"The Leyak Queen Spells","Your patron's magic keeps certain spells always ready for you. When you reach a Warlock level shown below, you gain the spells listed for that level, and from then on you always have them prepared. **Warlock Level 3.** Bane, Ray of Sickness, Blindness/Deafness, Hold Person. **Warlock Level 5.** Fear, Stinking Cloud. **Warlock Level 7.** Giant Insect, Polymorph. **Warlock Level 9.** Contagion, Hold Monster."],[3,"Leyak Form","As a Magic action, you transform parts of your body into the shape of a leyak, and your neck disappears while you are in this form. The form lasts for 10 minutes and grants you the following benefits. **Sharp Claws.** Your hands count as a Simple Melee weapon with the Finesse property that deals 1d8 Force damage. **Bonus Action Attack.** While in this form, you can take a Bonus Action to make one melee attack with a weapon that has the Finesse property or with an Unarmed Strike. **Mystical Resilience.** You have Resistance to a number of damage types equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one), chosen from Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing. Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Short Rest or a Long Rest."],[6,"Misfortune Bringer","When an attack you make with a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike hits a creature, you can force it to make a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC. If the save fails, the creature gains the Jinxed condition. Your uses of this feature equal your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and all spent uses return when you finish a Long Rest."],[10,"Grand Leyak","The gifts of your patron now fill you with a darker, more cursed power. While your Leyak Form is active, you gain whichever one of the following benefits you choose. **Deadly Claws.** The damage of your Sharp Claws becomes 1d10 Force. **Savage Monster.** Each time you take the Attack action on your turn, your Sharp Claws can make one additional attack. **Elusive Beast.** You gain the benefit of the Mage Armor spell."],[14,"Calon Arang","You have become the chosen prodigy of your patron, gaining the following benefits. **Otherworldly Resilience.** You have Immunity to two damage types of your choice from Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, and Thunder. **Extra Spell Slots.** Your number of Warlock spell slots increases by an amount equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). Unlike your other Warlock spell slots, these slots return only when you finish a Long Rest, not a Short Rest."]]},
  Wizard:{"School of Modernity":[[3,"Mixtape Spellbook","A portable cassette player can serve you as a spellbook. You can copy a spell from a spellbook into the cassette player in the same way you would copy a spell from one spellbook into another. When you gain this subclass, you can copy every Wizard spell in your spellbook into the cassette player, with no cost in gold and no time required."],[3,"Tech Wiz","Your grasp of modern technology is unmatched, granting you the following benefits. **Bonus Proficiency.** You gain proficiency in the Computer skill. **Fidgety Hands.** You can take the Utilize action with a Bonus Action."],[3,"Enspelled Cassette","As a Magic action, you can cast a Wizard spell of level 1 or higher that is in your Mixtape Spellbook and capture it on a cassette tape. The spell must have a casting time of an action or a Bonus Action. When that tape is played in any cassette player, the spell is cast, with the player acting as the caster and targeting itself. If the spell targets more than one creature, it picks the creatures nearest to the player first. The tape stays dormant for 8 hours, after which it becomes inert."],[6,"Funky Playlist","You can take a Utilize action with your Mixtape Spellbook to put the Deafened condition on yourself. While this feature keeps you Deafened, you gain the following benefits. **Tuned In.** Your spell save DC and spell attack bonus for Wizard spells each increase by 1. **In the Groove.** You have Advantage on attack rolls for the Wizard spells you cast. The Deafened condition from this feature ends if you take damage or if a creature takes a Utilize action to remove it."],[6,"Virtual Pet","You have learned to bring your familiar into the digital world, granting you the following benefits. **Bonus Spell.** Find Familiar is added to your Mixtape Spellbook. You always have it prepared, and it is not counted among the spells you prepare. **Digital Familiar.** When you cast Find Familiar, you can summon the familiar in the form of an EggBuddy device. **Wire Walker.** Your digital familiar can leap out of its own device into any other device no more than 5 feet away, or travel from one cable to another cable. Each jump gives off a faint electric crackle."],[10,"Device Upgrade","The bonus from your Funky Playlist feature to your Wizard spell save DC and Wizard spell attack bonus increases to 2."],[14,"Battery Charger","Your Arcane Recovery feature can now be used twice between Long Rests. In addition, you can use Arcane Recovery by taking a Magic action, instead of when you finish a Short Rest."]]}},
 subGrants:{"Pencak Silat":{unarmed:[[3,"1d8","1d6"],[10,"1d10","1d8"],[15,"1d12","1d10"]],flowing:["Dagger","Sickle","Shortsword"]},"Path of the Barong":{armor:[[3,"Heavy"]]},"College of Hymns":{tools:[[3,"Zither"]]},"School of Modernity":{skills:[[3,"Computer"]]},"Joystick":{tools:[[3,"All Gaming Sets"]]}},
 subChoices:{"Pencak Silat":[{l:3,k:"cunning",n:1,from:["Perception","Medicine"],title:"Cunning Eye skill",feature:"Close Quarter Combatant"}],"The Leyak Queen":[{l:10,k:"grand",n:1,kind:"opt",list:[["Deadly Claws","Sharp Claws deal 1d10 Force damage."],["Savage Monster","One extra Sharp Claws attack when you take the Attack action."],["Elusive Beast","You have the benefit of the Mage Armor spell."]],title:"Grand Leyak benefit",feature:"Grand Leyak"},{l:14,k:"imm",n:2,kind:"opt",list:[["Acid","Immunity to Acid damage."],["Cold","Immunity to Cold damage."],["Fire","Immunity to Fire damage."],["Lightning","Immunity to Lightning damage."],["Necrotic","Immunity to Necrotic damage."],["Poison","Immunity to Poison damage."],["Thunder","Immunity to Thunder damage."]],title:"Otherworldly Resilience: 2 damage types",feature:"Calon Arang",dres:"Immunity"}]},
 autoSpells:{"Oath of the Law":[[3,"Alarm,Command"],[5,"See Invisibility,Zone of Truth"],[9,"Dispel Magic,Remove Curse"],[13,"Guardian of Faith,Locate Creature"],[17,"Legend Lore,Wall of Force"]],"The Leyak Queen":[[3,"Bane,Ray of Sickness,Blindness/Deafness,Hold Person"],[5,"Fear,Stinking Cloud"],[7,"Giant Insect,Polymorph"],[9,"Contagion,Hold Monster"]],"School of Modernity":[[6,"Find Familiar"]]},
 skills:{Automotive:"WIS",Computer:"INT"},skillD:{"Automotive": "Automotive (Wisdom). Driving vehicles, repairing them, and understanding how they work.", "Computer": "Computer (Intelligence). Operating computers and understanding how their hardware and software work."},lore:[{"title": "A Young World", "text": "Retromistika is a world still in its childhood, only about four centuries old. It came into being when Yol Empah, the deity whose power kept the realms apart, was slain. With that sudden death, the land of Buana, the sky of Kalnis, and the sea of Shia collided and fused together. War broke out almost at once, as the mortals of each realm fought over who could claim what. Peace came only after two hundred bitter years of fighting, when every side finally reached an agreement.\n\nFrom then on, Retromistika began to change and reshape itself into what it is today: three realms living side by side in what looks like harmony. Yet calm surfaces can hide great depths. How deep do these waters run when not even the horizon can hold them? And how long before the sky unleashes a storm while the land sinks beneath an ocean that will not stir?"}, {"title": "What to Expect", "text": "Retromistika takes place in a world not far from our own. Its inspiration is Indonesia in the 1980s together with the mysticism of Nusantara, blended with a history that has taken a few more fantastical turns.\n\nThe world is also passing through an odd period of transition. Technology is advancing at great speed and is slowly pulling away from both nature and magic. How that works in a world so closely bound to nature and the spirits is something the authors will hint at and everyone at the table will discover together. They hope players feel welcome here, though not too welcome, because nobody knows what may be hiding among the trees."}, {"title": "Origins", "text": "Four hundred years have gone by since the Coalescence. Buana itself, however, is far older than that, and so are Kalnis and Shia. They existed before the first thought was ever formed, back when they were simply separate places in separate times.\n\nUncounted ages ago, the world came into being. At the very moment of its creation, before it had even settled, deities such as Yol Empah came into existence. While the gods were shaping their own forms and their domains together, the world brought forth the many spirits and creatures that still live in it. First came the plants, then the divine spirits, then the lesser spirits, and finally the mortals and the animals. For millennia now forgotten, life, nature, and harmony flourished across the realms.\n\nFor all that age, the oldest written record dates back only 2,400 years. Anything earlier survives only in oral tradition or in what the older spirits are willing to share, and there is no promise that the spirits ever told the truth. For practical purposes, the history before that point is lost."}, {"title": "Calendar: BC and AD", "text": "Retromistika counts its years in two eras. BC stands for Before Coalescence, and AD stands for After Death. The dividing line is the slaying of Yol Empah, who by then was the last of the deities. Once Yol Empah was dead, nothing kept the realms apart, and Kalnis and Shia crashed down into Buana. That event is called the Coalescence.\n\nThe BC era is divided into two halves, each named after the Reksa te Buana, or ruler of the land, who held power then. The earlier half is the Era of Mahagrita Wakasha, which ran from 1990 BC to 1578 BC. The later half is the Era of Paithak Kho Thee, which ran from 1577 BC to 1 BC."}, {"title": "The Two Reksas", "text": "There is much to say about each Reksa, but people generally recall the Era of Wakasha as one that leaned toward nature. Mahagrita Wakasha worked for peaceful coexistence between the spirits and the Mistikans within what was then modern Buana society. He is also remembered for fighting to make iskars accepted, both the word itself and the profession it names.\n\nThe Era of Paithak Kho Thee, in contrast, put Mistikans at the center of everything. Modern civilization expanded at a fierce pace. Forests, hills, open land, and even some mountains were cleared or seized so that cities could rise on them. During his rule, the seven divine spirits struck at Himagupta and other cities more than once. Even so, his era is remembered above all for a single event: the death of Yol Empah and the Coalescence that followed."}, {"title": "The War and the Peace", "text": "After the Coalescence, the merged world plunged into an enormous war that went on for 200 years. So much of the joined world was ruined or damaged along the way that, with little left to build on, everyone had to learn how to live alongside one another. Negotiations took place and peace was reached, though tensions stayed high. Most of the world was simply too tired of fighting, so hardly anyone resisted once peace was proposed. Instead, people threw themselves into rebuilding. New cities were designed to accommodate creatures from Shia and Kalnis, and the peoples of every realm began to mix.\n\nIn AD 205, the current Reksa te Buana took office: a Buana Mistikan named Wuliyanto Mokhla, who has ruled ever since. The present year is AD 485. Society has grown much more harmonious, yet in certain ways the world could be said to be more divided than ever."}, {"title": "Society", "text": "Life in Retromistika is at once simple and complicated. It is simple because anything and anyone can find a place in it. Spirits such as kuyangs and begu ganjangs, among many others, live and work just like Retrons and Mistikans of every ancestry. It is complicated because a constant tension hangs in the air. Two hundred years or so is not long enough for a society to heal completely. By the divine spirits, everyone is doing their best, but effort alone can achieve only so much without time on its side."}, {"title": "Daily Life", "text": "A typical citizen is usually awake and moving by seven or eight in the morning. They eat breakfast at the neighborhood warung, a small shop, and pick up lunch while riding to work on their Apsara model vehicle. Some have to catch the train or take a water lift to get where they are going. Everyone in Retromistika simply lives side by side, doing their work, eating, and going to bed, only to repeat it all the next day. Seen that way, it may be fair to call this civilization both simple and harmonious."}]}};
