HB_BUILTIN.pilgungy={"id": "pilgungy", "name": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya (Homebrew)", "loreLabel": "Rules", "desc": "Rules of the Aurvidya setting, written by the game master Pilgungy (Panduan Bermain: Abu Purba Aurvidya, Panduan Pemain: Bunga untuk Sang Raja): Bonus Class Features at level 3, Masterwork Weapons, Combat Maneuver Roll.", "clsFeat": {"Barbarian": [[3, "Roar of Cou-Rage", "When you enter your Rage, every ally within 60 feet of you who can hear your roar can immediately make a new saving throw, with Advantage, to end each Charmed or Frightened condition affecting it.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "When you enter your Rage, every ally within 60 feet of you who can hear your roar can immediately make a new saving throw, with Advantage, to end each Charmed or Frightened condition affecting it. If your roar helps at least one ally this way, you and every ally you helped gain a 1d6 bonus to your next D20 Test. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Bard": [[3, "Final Inspiration", "After you have spent your last use of Bardic Inspiration, on your next turn you can give up one of your Hit Point Dice, without taking an action, to gain a d12 Bardic Inspiration die that you can use.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "After you have spent your last use of Bardic Inspiration, on your next turn you can give up one of your Hit Point Dice, without taking an action, to gain a d12 Bardic Inspiration die that you can use. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Cleric": [[3, "Lesser Intervention", "You can spend one use of your Channel Divinity to cast a spell from the Cleric spell list of level 3 or lower, as long as the spell's casting time is not a Reaction.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "You can spend one use of your Channel Divinity to cast a spell from the Cleric spell list of level 3 or lower, as long as the spell's casting time is not a Reaction. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Druid": [[3, "Adept Beast Tongue", "You can cast Speak with Animals without spending a spell slot.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "You can cast Speak with Animals without spending a spell slot. You can do so once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest. In addition, when you cast that spell, you can also use it to communicate with monsters that resemble beasts."}]], "Fighter": [[3, "Secure Wind", "When an attack scores a Critical Hit against you, you can take a Reaction and spend one use of your Second Wind to cancel the extra effect of that Critical Hit, and you also regain Hit Points from your Second Wind as normal.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "When an attack scores a Critical Hit against you, you can take a Reaction and spend one use of your Second Wind to cancel the extra effect of that Critical Hit, and you also regain Hit Points from your Second Wind as normal. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Monk": [[3, "Deflect Energy (Aurvidya)", "By spending 1 Focus Point, you can use your Deflect Attacks feature against an attack that deals any type of damage other than Psychic.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "By spending 1 Focus Point, you can use your Deflect Attacks feature against an attack that deals any type of damage other than Psychic. Your uses of this feature equal your Proficiency Bonus, and all spent uses return when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Paladin": [[3, "Channeling Smite", "When you hit a target with a melee attack, using either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one use of your Channel Divinity to cast Divine Smite, or another level 1 Smite spell that you have prepared, without spending a spell slot or your Bonus Action.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "When you hit a target with a melee attack, using either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can spend one use of your Channel Divinity to cast Divine Smite, or another level 1 Smite spell that you have prepared, without spending a spell slot or your Bonus Action. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Ranger": [[3, "Favored Ally", "Animal Friendship is always prepared for you and is not counted among the spells you prepare.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "Animal Friendship is always prepared for you and is not counted among the spells you prepare. You can spend one use of your Favored Enemy feature to cast Animal Friendship without spending a spell slot. For the duration of a spell cast this way, you and the Beast it targets share a telepathic link that lets you communicate with each other. A Beast whose Challenge Rating is lower than your total character level automatically fails its saving throw against that spell. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Rogue": [[3, "Uncanny Mind", "When you fail an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, you can turn the failure into a success.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "When you fail an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma saving throw, you can turn the failure into a success. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Sorcerer": [[3, "Meta-Spell", "While your Innate Sorcery is active, you can apply two Metamagic options to a spell you are about to cast, paying only the Sorcery Point cost of whichever of the two options costs more.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "While your Innate Sorcery is active, you can apply two Metamagic options to a spell you are about to cast, paying only the Sorcery Point cost of whichever of the two options costs more. You can use this feature once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Warlock": [[3, "Warlock's Mantra", "Choose one level 1 spell from the Warlock spell list that has a Verbal component and that you have prepared.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "Choose one level 1 spell from the Warlock spell list that has a Verbal component and that you have prepared. You can cast the chosen spell without spending a spell slot or a Pact Magic slot. Your uses equal your Charisma modifier, and all spent uses return when you finish a Long Rest."}]], "Wizard": [[3, "Arcanic Formula", "Through long study, you have mastered one spell that wizards rarely know.", {"hb": "DM Pilgungy: Aurvidya", "full": "Through long study, you have mastered one spell that wizards rarely know. Choose one spell that has at least a Verbal and a Somatic component and whose level is one you have spell slots for. You always have the chosen spell prepared, and you can cast it without spending a spell slot. You can do so once, and you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest. You can swap the chosen spell for a different one only when you gain a level."}]]}, "clsSpells": {"Druid": [[3, "Speak with Animals", "1/Long Rest free", "Adept Beast Tongue"]], "Ranger": [[3, "Animal Friendship", "Always prepared", "Favored Ally"]]}, "spellPick": {"Warlock": {"l": 3, "key": "hbMantra", "title": "Warlock's Mantra: a prepared level 1 Warlock spell with a Verbal component", "lv": 1, "list": "Warlock", "comp": "V", "use": "Warlock's Mantra, no slot", "feature": "Warlock's Mantra", "prep": 1}, "Wizard": {"l": 3, "key": "hbFormula", "title": "Arcanic Formula: spell with Verbal and Somatic components", "slots": 1, "comp": "V,S", "use": "Always prepared, 1/Long Rest free", "feature": "Arcanic Formula"}}, "items": [["Battleaxe, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Battleaxe. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Topple, 4 lb.", {"base": ["Battleaxe"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 110}], ["Dagger, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Dagger. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Nick, 1 lb.", {"base": ["Dagger"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 102}], ["Dart, Masterwork (20)", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Dart. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Vex, 5 lb.", {"base": ["Dart"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 101}], ["Flail, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Flail. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Sap, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Flail"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 110}], ["Glaive, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Glaive. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Graze, 6 lb.", {"base": ["Glaive"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 120}], ["Greataxe, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Greataxe. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Cleave, 7 lb.", {"base": ["Greataxe"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 130}], ["Greatsword, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Greatsword. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Graze, 6 lb.", {"base": ["Greatsword"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 150}], ["Halberd, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Halberd. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Cleave, 6 lb.", {"base": ["Halberd"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 120}], ["Handaxe, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Handaxe. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Vex, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Handaxe"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}], ["Heavy Crossbow, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Heavy Crossbow. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Push, 18 lb.", {"base": ["Heavy Crossbow"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 150}], ["Javelin, Masterwork (10)", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Javelin. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Slow, 20 lb.", {"base": ["Javelin"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}], ["Light Hammer, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Light Hammer. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Nick, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Light Hammer"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 102}], ["Mace, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Mace. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Sap, 4 lb.", {"base": ["Mace"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}], ["Sickle, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Sickle. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Nick, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Sickle"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 101}], ["Lance, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Lance. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Topple, 6 lb.", {"base": ["Lance"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 110}], ["Longsword, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Longsword. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Sap, 3 lb.", {"base": ["Longsword"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 115}], ["Maul, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Maul. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Topple, 10 lb.", {"base": ["Maul"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 110}], ["Morningstar, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Morningstar. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Sap, 4 lb.", {"base": ["Morningstar"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 115}], ["Pike, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Pike. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Push, 18 lb.", {"base": ["Pike"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}], ["Rapier, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Rapier. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Vex, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Rapier"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 125}], ["Scimitar, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Scimitar. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Nick, 3 lb.", {"base": ["Scimitar"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 125}], ["Shortsword, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Shortsword. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Vex, 2 lb.", {"base": ["Shortsword"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 110}], ["Trident, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Trident. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Topple, 4 lb.", {"base": ["Trident"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}], ["Warhammer, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made Warhammer. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Push, 5 lb.", {"base": ["Warhammer"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 115}], ["War Pick, Masterwork", "Weapon", "Not magic", 0, "A finely made War Pick. It is not magic. +1 to attack rolls made with it. Mastery Sap, 2 lb.", {"base": ["War Pick"], "fx": {"atk": 1, "mw": 1}, "cost": 105}]], "cmr": 1, "lore": [{"title": "Variant Rule: Bonus Class Features", "text": "**Variant Rule: Bonus Class Features.** In the 2024 rules there are twelve classes to choose from. Under this variant, used in every adventure set in Aurvidya, each class gains one extra ability at level 3, listed below. Each ability belongs to its class and is gained alongside that class's normal level 3 features."}, {"title": "Masterwork Weapons", "text": "**Masterwork Weapons.** Masterwork weapons are the signature line of the smiths of the Dema Kingdom, sold in Andros Demascus's forge shop. A Masterwork weapon is not a magic weapon, so it can still be the target of spells such as Magic Weapon. A Masterwork weapon grants a +1 bonus to every attack roll made with it. It costs 100 GP more than the ordinary version of the same weapon. Its mastery property and weight are the same as the ordinary weapon."}, {"title": "Combat Maneuver Roll", "text": "**Combat Maneuver Roll.** This is a variant combat rule. When a feature of a martial class would impose a nonmagical effect on an opponent and calls for that opponent to make a Strength or Dexterity saving throw, the creature performing the maneuver can instead make a Combat Maneuver Roll. **Roll.** 1d20 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. **Difficulty Class.** The roll is compared against a Difficulty Class based on the target: 8 plus the target's Proficiency Bonus plus its Strength modifier plus its Dexterity modifier. If your roll meets or beats that number, the maneuver's effect applies as though the target had failed its saving throw."}]};
